---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import PageHeader from '../../components/PageHeader.astro';
import Section from '../../components/Section.astro';
import { site } from '../../data/site';
const updated = '2026-09-06';
---
<Base
  title="Privacy notice"
  description="How Carbon Project Australia collects, uses and stores personal information submitted through carbonproject.ai."
>
  <PageHeader
    eyebrow="Legal"
    title="Privacy notice"
    lede={`How we handle information you send us through this site. Last updated ${updated}.`}
    crumbs={[]}
  />

  <Section rule={false}>
    <div class="flow legal">
      <p class="muted">
        {site.legalName} (“we”, “us”) is an Australian company. This notice explains what we do with
        personal information collected through <strong>carbonproject.ai</strong>. We handle personal
        information in accordance with the <em>Privacy Act 1988</em> (Cth) and the Australian Privacy
        Principles.
      </p>

      <h2>What we collect</h2>
      <p>We collect only what you choose to send us:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Your name, work email address and organisation, if you enter them in the enquiry form.</li>
        <li>The content of your enquiry, including anything you choose to describe in the brief field.</li>
        <li>Any information you send us by email.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        We do not run advertising trackers, we do not set marketing cookies, and we do not sell,
        rent or share your information with data brokers.
      </p>

      <h2>Why we collect it</h2>
      <p>
        To answer your enquiry, to prepare a scope or quote if you ask for one, and to keep a record
        of our dealings with you. If we later want to send you anything that is not a reply to your
        enquiry, we will ask first, and every such message will carry a working unsubscribe.
      </p>

      <h2>Where it goes</h2>
      <p>
        Enquiries submitted through the form are delivered to our email and, where a form-handling
        service is used, pass through that service in transit. Correspondence is stored in our
        business systems. We use reputable providers and we do not transfer personal information
        overseas for the purpose of processing your enquiry beyond what those mail and form services
        require to deliver it.
      </p>
      <p>
        Client data handled under a services agreement is a separate matter. Where we run inference,
        fine-tuning or facility work for you, the handling of that data is governed by the written
        data-handling schedule attached to that agreement, which names the site, the retention period
        and the access list. This notice does not override it.
      </p>

      <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
      <p>
        Enquiries are kept while there is a live commercial conversation and for as long as we
        reasonably need them afterwards for business records. You can ask us to delete an enquiry at
        any time and we will, unless we are required to keep it.
      </p>

      <h2>Analytics and cookies</h2>
      <p>
        This site does not set cookies and does not load third-party analytics or advertising
        scripts. Our host keeps standard server request logs for security and operational purposes.
      </p>

      <h2>Security</h2>
      <p>
        We take reasonable steps to protect personal information from misuse, loss and unauthorised
        access. No transmission over the internet is completely secure, so please do not send
        classified, clearance-controlled or highly sensitive material through the enquiry form — ask
        us for an appropriate channel instead.
      </p>

      <h2>Access, correction and complaints</h2>
      <p>
        You may ask us what personal information we hold about you, ask us to correct it, or complain
        about how we have handled it. Email <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a> and we
        will respond within a reasonable period, ordinarily within 30 days.
      </p>
      <p>
        If you are not satisfied with our response you can complain to the Office of the Australian
        Information Commissioner at
        <a href="https://www.oaic.gov.au" rel="noopener">oaic.gov.au</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>
        We will update this page if our practices change, and the date at the top will change with
        it.
      </p>
    </div>
  </Section>
</Base>

<style>
  .legal { max-width: var(--measure); }
  .legal h2 { font-size: var(--step-1); }
  .legal a { color: var(--action); }
  .legal strong { font-weight: 600; }
</style>
